    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0677" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg621"/>

                <head>No. 350.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dart
                        to Mr. Cadwalader.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate General of the United States of America for the British
                                North American Provinces</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Montreal</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 25, 1876</date>.
                        (Received April 27, 1876.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that, on
                    examining the petition of appeal in case of Charles Worms, that document does
                    not raise the points material in the discussion with Great Britain. Those points
                    were raised on the argument upon the return to the writ of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">habeas corpus</hi>.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I transmit herewith a copy of Justice Dorion’s return to the supreme court of
                    Canada in that case.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM A. DART,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Consul-General</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d349-a1.xml" xpointer="d349-a1"/>
